# Range-delete walks closed per shard: each shard's walk is stamped with its own
# shard's routing generation, so this shard's close re-claims only its own. Another
# shard's walk, still in flight after its fan-out was abandoned, is allocated above
# the heads this shard's close recorded, and L's leaf, which replays every
# overlapping range-delete record, re-arms and passes it.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestRangeDeletePerShardClose
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: another shard's range-delete walk is not fenced by this shard's close
PERTURBS: GAlloc
BOUNDS: WithTreeWalk = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ gst = "pend"
    /\ gstamp >= fFence
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- REPLACE
    /\ gst = "pend"
\* MUTATION: stamped with its own shard's generation, which L's close does not re-claim.
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- END